{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players","id":902486,"title":"Challenging Human Supremacy in HtV Players","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-28T21:45:48-07:00","id":902486,"title":"Challenging Human Supremacy in HtV Players","content":"Whether the setting is fantasy or science fiction, if it involves humans meeting with non-humans, there is a sub-genre which, at least in the eyes of its fans, is dedicated to emphasizing the superiority and unquenchable moral rightness of humanity. On /tg/ boards, this motif is called &quot;Humanity, Fuck Yeah!&quot;, but to avoid getting banned by the mods for excessive swearing, I've gone for the hopefully less incendiary stand in of &quot;human supremacy&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now, human supremacists interested in the Chronicles of Darkness setting just love Hunter: The Vigil, seeing it as basically a celebration of their ideology. This is often called into contrast with Hunter: The Reckoning, which, as part of the World of Darkness, essentially went with the opposite viewpoint of &quot;humanity is weak&quot; - take in note that Reckoning!Hunters were only made capable of going toe-to-toe with the creatures of the night because they were empowered by mystical patrons of good, whilst Vigil!Hunters are ordinary humans (for the most part) taking on the creatures of the night with grit, guts and guns.<br /> <br /> Now, I'll be the first to admit that the Chronicles do explicitly have a more positive depiction of humanity than the WoD did. However, it's not taken to the extent that &quot;being human is being perfect; being nonhuman is an abomination&quot;. The gamelines that do explicitly have some strong human-positive or pro-humanity viewpoints are given valid reasons for doing so - Promethean, for example, isn't so much &quot;humanity is perfection&quot; as it is &quot;humans are flawed, but still better than being an outcast with no place in creation&quot;, whilst vampires try to cling to their humanity since they're basically el cheapo knockoffs of werewolves, with predatory natures clumsily grafted to minds incapable of really handling them and given Kuruth with faulty safety valves.<br /> <br /> Even in Hunter itself, care is taken to avoid being too pro-humanity. Though others have complained on these very forums about, say, Les Mysteres being puppets of the spirits or the Keepers of the Source being misguided about the way that Essence works, I think groups like them have a very real place in the rulebooks. Even if their specific execution can leave things to be desired in my eyes, they still emphasize that being a hunter does <b>not</b> ensure you are in the right. Hunters will get things wrong, they will get blindsided, they will get subverted, swayed, duped or corrupted. In other words, <i><b>hunters are not infallible</b></i>.<br /> <br /> And yet, somehow, players seem to keep coming to Hunter from that human supremacist viewpoint. Why it is that this is so, I really don't know. Does the specific &quot;you are humans who dare to bump back against the things going bump in the night&quot; seem to just overpower the statements of the Chronicles being a &quot;horrifying world of dark mystery&quot;? Did I miss some memo that the Chronicles' general rule of moral ambiguity and &quot;Black &amp; Grey Morality&quot; was suspended in Hunter games? I don't really know, and I don't really care.<br /> <br /> I confess a certain intense distaste for the human supremacy theme in general. But, in particular, it bugs me to sit down to a game of Hunter expecting an action horror game in the world that the rest of the Chronicles have sold me on, and then the game turns into a bog-standard &quot;black &amp; white morality slashfest with minor horror trappings&quot;, ala the stereotype of D&amp;D horror games.<br /> <br /> So, I had a burning desire to ask: has anyone else ever noticed this tendency in their Hunter games? If so, how have you challenged it? How have you addressed the topic of conveying to players that &quot;no, being human fighting monsters does not make you an action hero with Omniscient Morality; it makes you at best a Bryonic Hero and at worse a kool-aid drinking member of the KKK&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T21:57:44-07:00","id":902490,"title":"","content":"Hunter to me is a game about two things: being horrifically outgunned by awful monsters, and the massive personal cost of upholding the Vigil instead of keeping your head down like a smart/sane person would. I feel like any Storyteller that isn't stressing those points is missing something vital to the game, but maybe I'm crazy. <br /> <br /> I think part of the reason Hunter has that unfortunate reputation you describe is due to its role as many non-horror gamers introduction to the CofD; many folks jump straight from D&amp;D to Hunter, and see it as more &quot;more murderhoboing, but in the modern day!&quot; rather than &quot;Delta Green versus the Universal movie monsters.&quot; It basically boils down to narrative immaturity, at least in my eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T22:33:46-07:00","id":902493,"title":"","content":"My Hunter games tend to focus on the hard moral questions of the Vigil, and (for tier 3) emphasizing the underlying hypocrisy and questioning ones own humanity. Characters with &quot;if it's not human it needs to die&quot; attitudes usually end up either reconsidering their position or on the slippery slope to Slasher-dome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T23:14:38-07:00","id":902504,"title":"","content":"Why challenge it? If everyone is having fun what's the problem?<br /> <br /> The Hunter setting doesn't demand moral greyness. The MM killing witches just for being witches, pretty dark. Killing vampires just for being vampires, pretty grey. The Union defending their community - pretty heroic*. If you want to play a humanity fuck yeah game, play a more heroic group and stick to lower powered antagonists like Thamaturges or Ghouls.<br /> <br /> And heck, if a group wants to kill Werewolves left right and center then who cares. If they're having fun they're having fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now if you're not having fun and your group is, just talk to them. Maybe you can reach a compromise, maybe you're just in the wrong group. But there's no <i>one weird trick</i> for this. You have to just talk to the group.<br /> <br /> * Howard Wood Ingham has gone on record on RPG.net saying that he wrote The Union as heroes. Later authors added some darkness like xenophobia, but corebook Union were supposed to be heroic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players#post902486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">, I think groups like them have a very real place in the rulebooks.</div> </div> </div> </div> They sure do! It's the antagonist chapter.<br /> <br /> I'm being completely serious. This is a quote from Hunter's introduction &quot;The theme here is \u201clight in shadows,\u201d with hunters being a reckoning force that takes action against the darkness.&quot;<br /> <br /> Serving or being unwitting pawns of monsters like Les Mysteries goes against that theme. However the setting demands it, it would outright break my suspension of disbelief if they weren't there. But that combination of anti-thematic and setting-required says to me &quot;put it in the antagonist chapter&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T08:13:48-07:00","id":902726,"title":"","content":"I have personally taken the stance that even at the most horribly flawed they can be, organizations in Hunter are still doing a just and noble thing. At lower rungs in a conspiracy, you can argue that the hunters are protecting innocent people with the caveat of having a bureaucracy to deal with.<br /> <br /> Speaking as someone who honestly prefers hunters in Humanity Fuck Yeah stories, I don't see how any hunter gains some kind of unquestioned moral supremacy. Instead, it always feels more like hunters convincing themselves (For the more heroic groups) that what they do is the necessary evil. As mentioned by Kings, there are some groups that are unambiguously heroic. That doesn't mean they shouldn't do what's necessary (Which if I remember correctly is one of the bigger themes in Princess).<br /> <br /> As for the Antagonist organizations, there are really two ways about it (For me at least). The first is that they are fooling themselves, like saying the Abe is really just desperately trying to find a way to give some sense of morality when they clearly are already way down the slippery slope as an organization. The second, and again this is just me, is to rewrite the organization. CofD is a toolkit after all. If I want Les Mysteries to be in actual confederation with spirits rather than being dupes, I can.<br /> <br /> Finally, this all seems to be more of a personal preference question. Like I said, I prefer HFY. I like having stories where Union members break a witch's kneecaps for summoning demons, stories where the Malleus and TFV force themselves to work together in order to destroy the apocalypse cult summoning Cthulu's second cousin. And to be honest, HFY seems way less incendiary than the unfortunate implications of using &quot;human supremacy&quot; in its place when discussing the concept. It seems more like the difference between HFY and Van Helsing Hate Crimes, which is already covered anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T09:45:44-07:00","id":902768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players?p=902504#post902504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why challenge it? If everyone is having fun what's the problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> Players know how difficult it is when they actually play. If some anonymous collective of people want to think hunters are the saviors of the universe, or even wants to run games where it's true, good for them. It has no bearing on the game itself or how I run it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T13:29:17-07:00","id":902975,"title":"","content":"No, it's not a problem that people can play the game that way when they want it. If the whole group wants it, then, as the last three posters have said, that's fine; so long as people are having fun.<br /> <br /> It <i>is</i> a problem when <i>some</i> of the group cling to that interpretation, despite the storyteller and the rest of the group wanting to do otherwise, and then get disruptive when they aren't pandered to.<br /> <br /> I have no problems with Hunter for the major reason that it takes cares not to paint &quot;human = Automatically Right and Guaranteed Good Guy; non-human = Automatically Wrong and Guaranteed Bad Guy&quot; over the core text. You can play it that way if you like, and that's no harm, but how do you deal with it when some of the group want to play it that way and others - particularly the ST - don't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T14:16:17-07:00","id":902998,"title":"","content":"Ah.<br /> <br /> Talk to the players one on one, try to make sure they understand the metagame. If you keep having troubles, talk to the group and look over what you put down for the chronicle. As hard as it can be to see, it's possible that you as the ST didn't get the point across clearly. Failing all that, maybe bag the current idea and bring up a new one with a more defined tone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T14:24:38-07:00","id":903005,"title":"","content":"Is excessive swearing a problem? How the fuck did I make it this long, then?<br /> <br /> EDIT Anyways, the problem.<br /> <br /> 1) Don't let the hunters only see black and white. THe monster's they hunt are people too, and while the worst of the bunch are more likely to be visible, keep in mind the behavior of players characters and use that to inform your antagonists and misdirections.<br /> <br /> 2) Hunters get used by monsters as much as not, and there's a variety of ways to do that. Find subtle ways to show they're in the game the monsters play as pieces rather than as players. It should still be to their advantage of course, but it should also demonstrate a sense of smallness.<br /> <br /> 3) Never be afraid to scare the living shit out of them and to design scenarios where the only answer is to run. While it is a fallacy, people do conflate might with right, and giving players a few good no-win scenarios will give them reason to doubt, reason to fear. It also tends to be very memorable scenes for players, because it's high-tension, player-praying-over-their-dice action that gets the blood going. It also makes places where they win also more poignant by comparison.<br /> <br /> 4) Keep other hunters in competition. Play up territorial behaviors, arrogance, greed, distrust, aggression, paranoia-run the whole gamut. Never let your PC hunters be the only ones in the picture, and always find a way to use them to make the PC's question themselves by comparison to their peers. Hunters should fight hunters almost as much as monsters.<br /> <br /> 5) Also keep pushing the buttons of the internal dynamics of the group. While you might not want to push it so far as to be lead to permanent divisions unless you have a group that enjoys that, PC's flaws stand out the most and affect the presence of human flaws more than any other characters.<br /> <br /> Just some thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-29-2016, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T23:53:28-07:00","id":903305,"title":"","content":"Flyboy has the right of it.<br /> <br /> The only possible solution is to talk to them out of charachter. If they're disruptive when they're not pandered too imagine how disruptive they'll be when people intentionally try to &quot;disrupt&quot; them by shaking up the setting with evil Hunters.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-30-2016, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T11:43:22-07:00","id":903685,"title":"","content":"As mentioned, I would say the issue is less with the players having a H,FY! attitude than them being disruptive when that view isn't catered to. Sometimes you have to find a different game. I've played in a W:tA game where it seemed any attempts to suggest moral grays were quashed by the STs, but other people were having fun so rather than make a thing of it I just bowed out. I've played in a C:tL game where I felt the themes of abuse were being overemphasized to the point of being oppressive, but other people were having fun so rather than make a thing of it I just bowed out. <br /> <br /> In Hunter there is room for H.FY! monster slaying and there is room for complex ethical questioning about the nature of humanity versus monstrosity. You just have to get a group and a game that's going to go for one of those. If not everyone is you have to either find a middle course or, sometimes, find a new game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T10:13:02-07:00","id":904240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players#post902486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I miss some memo that the Chronicles' general rule of moral ambiguity and &quot;Black &amp; Grey Morality&quot; was suspended in Hunter games?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! I love answering rhetorical questions where the person doesn't care to hear an answer, sarcasm aside and very sincerely, thank you for the opportunity.<br /> <br /> While it is possible to play the 'human supremacy' motif in the Hunter: The Vigil you'd have to completely ignore the themes covering descent into becoming Slashers and the numerous serial killer/Vigil!Hunter comparisons throughout the all books talking about monster hunters (emotes eyeing the <i>Antagonists </i>Core <i>Hunter: The Vigil</i> and <i>Slashers</i> books), or at least suffer some moderate mental dissonance.The whole Slasher phenomenon refutes moral blank and white 'Human Supremacy' as a theme intended for the game line.<br /> <br /> So you missed no memo, and 'Human Supremacy' is not a theme inherent in Hunter the Vigil, but rather something grafted on by those that favor that mindset in the first place. While there is room for Hunter's thinking of themselves as &quot;heroes&quot; initially, depending on compact, it should become clear at some point in the chronicle in the larger world that merely being human doesn't make you less monstrous than a supernatural creature, or even that every supernatural creature is even a monster. Cheiron Group and Ashwood Abby strike me as two of the easiest examples of compacts that can be painted in such a light that they seem worse than at least some monsters. Even if the specific cell the players belong to can maintain moral high ground itself, the fact other humans are more obscene than supposed abominations should remove the trope of the overall superiority of humanity.<br /> <br /> Also about problem players, I recommend pointing out the above out of character, and then perhaps give them a list of themes you intend to cover in your game so they have the option to buy-in, or opt out. I find the best games happen with people working towards a goal shared than adversarial, and I f you need to shift the cast of your players to have the game you want, please know you are the one investing Storyteller time and effort and recruit a player base that meets the needs of what you want to run.<br /> <br /> That being said, friendships have value and just because people don't share exactly the same taste in fiction doesn't mean relationships have to be lost, only perhaps the activity and who invests what may need to change.<br /> <br /> Of course this all happens in a white-room, and in my games supernatural creatures police themselves for the same reason humanity policies itself, it is made of real people, not mere caricatures, and real people care even though they are flawed and selfish. &quot;Monster Hunter&quot; is not a concept reserved in anyway for humans, and because of that my settings tend to be self-regulating. You may find having supernatural creatures hunting monstrous members of the various splats takes a good bit of wind out the bag of the supposed moral high ground of mortal hunters vs supernatural ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 05-31-2016, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T16:24:10-07:00","id":904539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players#post902486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">has anyone else ever noticed this tendency in their Hunter games? If so, how have you challenged it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, back then some of my players really liked Supernatural, and came with a similar mindset: If you are a monster that do even the slightest bad, like feeding only the bare minimum fresh brain to your children for it to survive until it grows enough to be able to eat days old corpse brain like you do, you are dead meat.<br /> <br /> I saw that as an opportunity to play that aspect, and show how monstrous they were becoming, the He Who Hunts Monsters trope. Of course, my players are very mature and open to interesting, dramatic moments, and it was pretty dramatic when they said &quot;Wait, what the F are we doing? We are supernatural-racists!&quot;. From there their characters started realizing how the other hunters and hunter cells acted exactly like they, the players, acted when they started the game. They realized that they were blinded by pride, fear, racism or pure joy, and they were actually pretty unhinged (at the time there was no Beast the Primordial, but in the end hunters started to look like beast's Heroes). It was a very deep, meta-level realization.<br /> <br /> Maybe stand-ins for ethnical issues, racism and armed militia aren't the default themes that HtV tries to focus, but I focused on that together with the issues of keeping a normal life together with the Vigil (something Supernatural almost never tries to do, except sometimes with the almost non-mary-sue character of Bobby), and they enjoyed it a lot.<br /> <br /> I think that in the end you don't <i>need</i> to shut down this player perspective. If it isn't just a immature power fantasy then you may do lots of things to this trope: You can <i>play</i> it straight or not, <i>subvert</i> it, <i>deconstruct</i> it, <i>lampshade </i>it... As long as it enriches your experience, why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11854,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","user":"DiBastet","date":". 05-31-2016, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T15:19:14-07:00","id":905218,"title":"","content":"My view of hunter has always been moral superiority over monsters is easy. Monsters are monsters after all. It's humans hunters morally falter to.<br /> <br /> So you burnt down the old abandoned church full of crazed bloodsuckers, easy win high fives all around.<br /> Well of course no one believes you and best case you're an arsonist, enjoy. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T20:42:14-07:00","id":905371,"title":"","content":"Always thought the idea that one might go overboard from 'the vigil' to 'rampant slayer of supernatural,' was a pretty important concept in hunter. They're both valid character motivations, and both allow for a lot of challenges, even if it doesn't seem that way at first. But the fun part, for me as a Storyteller, has always been in the possible turning point. Lots of corrupting influences, though I am fair about it.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/lfkSoUa.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I play with a pretty steady group, but while I've expanded a bit lately to newer groups I've never come up with a 'humanity fuck yeah' player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T17:42:53-07:00","id":906837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DiBastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players?p=904539#post904539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, back then some of my players really liked Supernatural, and came with a similar mindset: If you are a monster that do even the slightest bad, like feeding only the bare minimum fresh brain to your children for it to survive until it grows enough to be able to eat days old corpse brain like you do, you are dead meat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry if I'm derailing here, but man, were your players watching the same Supernatural I watched? Unless things changed significantly after Season 5, that show was always a great case study on why it's not that black and white. Dean often tries to treat it like it's that simple, and Sam tends to go too far in the opposite direction to the point of na\u00efvet\u00e9, and it always ends up biting them both in the ass. Besides, with Sam's whole demon-blooded, chosen vessel of Lucifer deal, he was a living example of exactly why it's not all &quot;monsters bad, people good&quot; and they regularly had to fight other hunters who were blind to shades of grey because of it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, swearing is fine. The books do it all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T01:47:03-07:00","id":907034,"title":"","content":"When running Hunter, or (hunter like) Mortal, I often try to have &quot;moral ambiguity&quot; such that it's not clear whether the Hunters are in the right or the wrong. My players killed the princes childe because one of the hunters was posessed by a Strix that decided he should have relations with her. This caused them to break a truce between Vampires and Hunters in the city. That said they were totally going for the attitude the OP describes. That said I feel like that &quot;human supremecy&quot; is that slippery slope of hunter that leads the hunter to becoming a monster (Slasher?). Just because a character/person believes they are on the side of &quot;right&quot; does not mean they actually are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 06-04-2016, 04:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T07:45:03-07:00","id":907629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players#post902486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">, whilst vampires try to cling to their humanity since they're basically el cheapo knockoffs of werewolves, with predatory natures clumsily grafted to minds incapable of really handling them and given Kuruth with faulty safety valves.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm sorry, but I just find this line to be rather amusing given the concern of this thread. A complaint about one splat having supremecy complex while demonstrating another. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T07:51:32-07:00","id":907635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players?p=906837#post906837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, swearing is fine. The books do it all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>For example, one of the werewolf abilities is literally called &quot;Badass Motherfucker&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T09:15:47-07:00","id":907668,"title":"","content":"Alright, I just wanted to thank everyone who has posted here for being so civil. Truth is, on reflection, I think I've been rather unnecessarily hostile towards you all, and I want to apologize for that.<br /> <br /> Really, I'm not having a problem with such disruptive players myself. And even if I do find the &quot;HFYeahists&quot; of Hunter somewhat annoying, that wasn't really what drove me to start this thread.<br /> <br /> I've always been of the opinion that part of what makes Hunter a horror game is the emphasis of how, no matter what you achieve, you are still a small fish in a big pond. You hold a candle against the darkness, but the darkness is bigger than you are, and patient. You will go out, eventually. But, what I struggle with is understanding how to convey that in a meaningful manner.<br /> <br /> How do you &quot;get across&quot; the theme of &quot;you're fighting back, but that doesn't guarantee you'll win&quot;? How do you make Hunter scary beyond the gore, the grotesqueries and the jump scares? Without doing something so blatantly unfair as &quot;that witch you whacked was actually the harmless goth-girl daughter of a REAL Moros, who promptly uses his magic to explode your hearts in revenge&quot;, how do you showcase just how powerful the creatures of the night are, and make the point that even with the candles of the Vigil, this is still, and may always be, a World of Darkness?<br /> <br /> That's ultimately what motivated me to come here and make this thread. I'm sorry for a misleading first post, and I'm sorry for all the attacks I've made on you posters during the course of this.<br /> <br /> <br /> @MCN<br /> Well, you have to admit, Humanity sucks a lot more for vampires than Harmony does for werewolves. The whole defining difference between the two is that Humanity focuses on holding *back* the influence of the Beast, whilst Harmony is about trying to keep Flesh and Spirit in check but accepting them as both equally important aspects of the whole.<br /> <br /> I'm not a huge fan of Humanity in 2e anyway - in contrast to Integrity or Harmony, it really does feel like a &quot;punishment stat&quot;. But that's off topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T09:49:47-07:00","id":907686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players?p=907668#post907668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no matter what you achieve, you are still a small fish in a big pond</div> </div> </div> </div> What's the point of having a distinction between Cells, Compacts and Conspiracies if you use the same themes for all of them?<br /> <br /> Cells are the small fish, Conspiracies are playing in the big leagues. Otherwise what's the point of having them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T11:16:44-07:00","id":907747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players?p=907635#post907635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, one of the werewolf abilities is literally called &quot;Badass Motherfucker&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Here's how you counter it:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i2.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/original/000/361/214/69a.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T13:53:00-07:00","id":907850,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4076-corvus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4076_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4076\" data-vbnamecard=\"4076\">Corvus</a> Rex:<br /> I see it more as a matter of scaling the threats up appropriately. Cell-tier? A coterie of vampires and the hints of covenants or bloodlines beyond are the reminder that there's more out there than you might be able to handle it. At Conspiracy-tier, you can easily handle vampires, even in small numbers... what keeps you up at night is the idea that there are *nations* of vampires out there, world-spanning conspiracies of blood-sucking monsters who manipulate the rise and fall of human civilization on a world level. A Conspiracy-tier hunter might not be afraid of a mage... but she *is* afraid of the Archmages, those inhuman gods who can erase her from history by sheer accident and not even notice.<br /> <br /> Big league players face big league opponents. You can ignore those chumps in the Union worrying about having Walker-Breaker the car-pain-death Magath running around when you're focused on keeping Irinam the Colossus, mad spirit of America, from wiping the slate clean with a barrage of natural disasters or provoking World War III.<br /> <br /> Hunter is a horror game first and foremost, or at least so I'm told. If being a Conspiracy hunter is when all the scary goes away, what's the point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T14:18:36-07:00","id":907873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players?p=907850#post907850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4076-corvus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4076_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4076\" data-vbnamecard=\"4076\">Corvus</a> Rex:<br /> At Conspiracy-tier, you can easily handle vampires, even in small numbers...</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, this is what most TF:V thinks. Cue evil laughter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T14:35:50-07:00","id":907889,"title":"","content":"Resiliance 5 won't let you survive even one airstirke <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players?p=907850#post907850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At Conspiracy-tier, you can easily handle vampires, even in small numbers... what keeps you up at night is the idea that there are *nations* of vampires out there, world-spanning conspiracies of blood-sucking monsters who manipulate the rise and fall of human civilization on a world level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that TF:V could take on the Inviticus and win. They're less divided by region, less backstabby, and they can operate during daytime.<br /> <br /> An Archmage, TF:V hasn't got a chance. But how often will an Archmage be even relevant to TF:V?<br /> <br /> <br /> More to the point though. If you just scale up the threat so that Conspiracies are still the underdog; then again. Why have the Conspiracy in the first place? Why not just play a Cell. An Ascending One (Knife of Paradise, the AO are really three different organisations) game should be one of diplomacy mixed in with the assassination of anyone who's not being &quot;reasonable&quot;. It's a fundamentally different feeling to playing the underdog - and without that difference, why have different organisations in the first place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T16:45:50-07:00","id":907975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players?p=907889#post907889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resiliance 5 won't let you survive even one airstirke <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I would say that TF:V could take on the Inviticus and win. They're less divided by region, less backstabby, and they can operate during daytime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Compacts and Conspiracies sourcebook would likely suppress that notion.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T18:02:04-07:00","id":908014,"title":"","content":"I'd get past human supremist vibe by reminding the players how often hunters die.<br /> <br /> Like lets be honest hunters likely have the most horrifying casualty rates of any splat in CoD, I mean look at how powerful, especially in CoD 2e, even a beginning character can be.<br /> <br /> And most splats are organized with a strong ability to gather intel on external threats.<br /> <br /> So I'd have the hunters run into the after math of other hunter cells being wiped out, rumours of entire conspiracies being wiped out completely by going to war with the wrong Supernatural Creatures, rumours of cities were almost all hunters have been wiped out, rumours that local governments have been taken over by supernatural creatuers,ect...<br /> <br /> I'd steal the betrayal system from Dark Eras New York Werewolves chapter to remind the players how easily hunters and other humans can be cooped by supernatural forces.<br /> <br /> Also have signs of high collateral damage. Burn down a building of vampires only to find out a spark of the fire started another one on an ophanage which also burned down with no survivors.<br /> <br /> You shoot a werewolve only to find the bullet exitted the werewolf and went right through the wall, killing the werewolf's neibour while he watched Jepordy.<br /> <br /> Kill a mage only to find out that he'd discovered the cure for cancer, but the chain saw you used to kill him, destroyed his formula.<br /> <br /> Kill a Changeling, only to find out that it was the fetch who you thought was human, was actually the mass murder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T02:13:00-07:00","id":908209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players?p=907975#post907975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Compacts and Conspiracies sourcebook would likely suppress that notion.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>... It wasn't that great a sourcebook. One of Hunter's core themes is basically &quot;United we Stand&quot;. While that means there's tons of story potential in &quot;Divided we Fall&quot;, C&amp;C didn't provide much material for playing a Conspiracy game where you play a game of United we Stand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T02:26:16-07:00","id":908213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players?p=908209#post908209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... It wasn't that great a sourcebook. One of Hunter's core themes is basically &quot;United we Stand&quot;. While that means there's tons of story potential in &quot;Divided we Fall&quot;, C&amp;C didn't provide much material for playing a Conspiracy game where you play a game of United we Stand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made no judgement on the quality of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T03:47:23-07:00","id":908239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players?p=907668#post907668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's ultimately what motivated me to come here and make this thread. I'm sorry for a misleading first post, and I'm sorry for all the attacks I've made on you posters during the course of this.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Were we attacked? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i><br /> <br /> Now on a slightly more serious tone, you might want to edit your original post or at least include an edit with your real intention then. There are kind-of-lurkers like me that don't care for reading the whole of replies before posting something and basically reply to the OP.<br /> <br /> Now, about your question... Well, i guess that boils down more to general horror GMing than HtV-specific advice. I think you might want to look for GMing advice on how to run horror games but mostly how to invoke <i>despair</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;1.noun loss of hope; hopelessness.<br /> 2.verb (used without object) someone or something that causes hopelessness: He is the despair of his mother.<br /> 3.verb (used with object) to lose, give up, or be without hope (often followed by of): to despair of humanity.<br /> 4. Obsolete. to give up hope of.&quot;<br /> <br /> There are many shades of hopelessness you might want to induce. You don't want to overdo it and end up with <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DarknessInducedAudienceApathy\" target=\"_blank\">Darkness-Induced Audience Apathy</a>, but if you are working on cell level things might get really close to that. I personally recommend TV Tropes, there are lots of examples and useful notes that might give you some inspiration.<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe take some notes from The Witcher games (I sure do). You usualy have choices to agonize over, but the game often deconstructs the idea of good choice or bad choice (and, perhaps sadistically, loves to subvert the &quot;third, hidden, better, middle choice&quot;), but more importantly, shows that while these choices influence the lives of people directly involved they don't change the bigger picture.<br /> <br /> <b>Case in point:</b><br /> At the beggining of the first game there is a hellhound (a powerful evil spirit), well... hounding... the village, picking people off and leaving their grisly remains. You have to deal with it in your stay there (but just because that's involved with your own search anyway). People in town are medieval moroms and racist, mud-covered assholes, and they blame a witch for cursing the town. You might think &quot;oh, it's probably not a <b>witch</b> witch, just a sage or something&quot;, but nope, it's a witch with dark practices a grudge on the asshole townspeople (that did bad things to her and that still come to her for help), with some poppets of the villagers and all, but that not only says she didn't summon a freaking hell-hound because that's impossible but also points that such a creature is drawn to evil, lots of evil (and later you found that's actually true). She still does black magic tho. You end up finding that lots of evil things that happened in the town and were blamed on the witch or other things were the works of pure evil human nature (a guy killed his own brother and buried his desecrated corpse on the yard to get his brother's fortune, for example). At a certain point the hellhound is still coming for the town, and the villagers -in a torch wielding mob form- cornered the witch on a cave. She begs for you to help her, and even offers herself to you to sweeten the deal (yeah, you might be <i>that</i> kind of asshole...). The villagers want to hang and / or burn her, but not before making her pay and torming / beating her. Then you have the choice to either<br /> <b>A)</b> Give the dark-magic practioner to the asshole mob, with predictable results.<br /> <b>B)</b> Protect her, with the protagonist saying this <i>&quot;You have two options. Wait until I leave and try to murder Abigail ... but then I'll come back. I'll slay every lice-ridden peasant, anything that moves and can't climb a tree. Or you can try to live honorable lives, clear your conscience, and start again. The choice is yours.&quot;.</i> The mob disperses but some of the men (including the asshole mayor) do come after you and you have to <i>kill them all</i> for real.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Nice story, DiBastet, but why is that example of lesser of two evils choice relevant?&quot;</i><br /> Well Jimmy, glad you asked. Because of the next part: The hellhound comes that night, as it did all nights before, and since everyone was outside, heading for their homes (either after burning the witch or because the mob dispersed), it dismembers and kills every single villager. Because of their bigotry they were stupid enough to be outside at night, thinking that killing a witch would fix their problems. They all die for that. It doesn't matter that you helped the witch or not, well, at least it only matters for the witch.<br /> <br /> I think that's a great example. The world of witcher is a terrible, evil world with evil monsters and evil people. You might kill a monster, solve a curse, or even find out that no supernatural monster did something but a deranged guy was killing people on the streets. But in the end you can only change the small picture. The lives of people that you interacte with. While there is a point to be made that by ridding the world of the threat you saved other people in the future, the story never allows itself to focus on that; the story gives the impression that everything you do is just a small, local stone. That colors your perception of the world and induces on the player the aura of despair that is all around setting. On the other hand the setting avoids complete apathy by focusing instead on the small picture, and the good things you did. You then weights that with all that you couldn't and can't accomplish, and sees why the main character is so sour and detached.<br /> <br /> Imagine this happened on a group's game. Sure, the villagers are all dead, ripped to pieces and scatered around for you to see, and while you did banish the supernatural hellhound, another similar evil spirit (or maybe this one comes back somehow) will surely come after the next town of evil assholes. BUT your group of hunters did <b>something</b>. Abigail is A) alive and saved from that cruel fate or B) dead like she deserves for being a evil witch. AND you guys might have lost some cell members ans maybe friends and contacts, but <b>this</b> hellhound's reign of terror is over.<br /> <br /> ...<i>yay</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11854,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","user":"DiBastet","date":". 06-06-2016, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T07:41:23-07:00","id":908331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players?p=908209#post908209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... It wasn't that great a sourcebook. One of Hunter's core themes is basically &quot;United we Stand&quot;. While that means there's tons of story potential in &quot;Divided we Fall&quot;, C&amp;C didn't provide much material for playing a Conspiracy game where you play a game of United we Stand.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are good things about C&amp;C and less than great things. Even moreso than TF:V's vampire connection (which I honestly don't mind that much), I think that EINHERJAR does them the most disservice as a playable organization. It seems primarily designed to either generate PVP or to make TF:V into NPC hunter antagonists, while simultaneously not making much sense even from the perspective of being a shady big government black ops outfit. The idea that TF:V would be compromised by making devil's bargains with nominally allied supernatural groups is something that jives perfectly well both with its status as a Conspiracy and as an entity in the world of clandestine intelligence. What doesn't make sense is that they would then turn around and give burn notices to every other hunter that isn't them.<br /> <br /> The way I run it is that EINHERJAR was a pilot program launched in Philadelphia that proved to be a catastrophic failure. Scrambling to salvage the op, it was subsequently reorganized a new mandate. EINHERJAR is now the the division that handles recruiting lower tier cells as deniable assets and informants, as well as overseeing all inter-agency cooperation between TF:V and the other Conspiracies to make sure classified shit stays classified and that everything stays within TF:V's overall interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T08:33:53-07:00","id":908356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players?p=908331#post908331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that TF:V would be compromised by making devil's bargains with nominally allied supernatural groups is something that jives perfectly well both with its status as a Conspiracy and as an entity in the world of clandestine intelligence.</div> </div> </div> </div> Absolutely. But it could be handled in far more interesting ways than it was. Instead of funding, I'd say TF:V worked with the Vampires in much the same way that cold-war USA worked with Osama bin Laden (possibly against the &quot;commie&quot; Free Council) and now it's come back to bite them in the ass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players?p=908331#post908331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I run it is that EINHERJAR was a pilot program launched in Philadelphia that proved to be a catastrophic failure. Scrambling to salvage the op, it was subsequently reorganized a new mandate. EINHERJAR is now the the division that handles recruiting lower tier cells as deniable assets and informants, as well as overseeing all inter-agency cooperation between TF:V and the other Conspiracies to make sure classified shit stays classified and that everything stays within TF:V's overall interest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. That's exactly what TF:V would do - though personally I'd drop the burn notice like pilot program and just say that TF:V always had a group dedicated to deniable assets and inter-agency cooperation; because of course they would.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T09:26:01-07:00","id":908380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players?p=908356#post908356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Absolutely. But it could be handled in far more interesting ways than it was. Instead of funding, I'd say TF:V worked with the Vampires in much the same way that cold-war USA worked with Osama bin Laden (possibly against the &quot;commie&quot; Free Council) and now it's come back to bite them in the ass.<br /> <br /> Makes sense. That's exactly what TF:V would do - though personally I'd drop the burn notice like pilot program and just say that TF:V always had a group dedicated to deniable assets and inter-agency cooperation; because of course they would.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There was a remark made earlier about TF:V taking on the Invictus, and my first thought was &quot;Why topple the Invictus when you can back a Carthian coup and accomplish the same thing?&quot;<br /> <br /> I only discuss the pilot program as a way of acknowledging that the version of EINHERJAR presented in Compacts &amp; Conspiracies did exist, rather than just sweeping it under the narrative rug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T20:19:25-07:00","id":909776,"title":"","content":"I've pretty much only run into &quot;Hunter Supremacy&quot; thing on the forums, primarily when people confuse their headcanon for what the books indicate, and a few people in my area who. . well, do the same thing. But the first is at least usually kinda interesting, and for the second I try to correct them (or at least make sure that they're making an informed decision to disregard the books) and if I either can't or they are, in fact, consciously deciding &quot;no thank you books&quot; then I don't run Hunter games for them and if I include Hunters in other games I run as antagonists, I make sure they're threatening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T11:09:38-07:00","id":910969,"title":"","content":"I never really thought of Hunter as advocating any human/hunter supremacy. The themes in the game seem to revolve around the person horror of discovering the unknown, just exactly what one might do when confronted with that knowledge, and kind of blindly stumbling around in the dark attempting to protect themselves and those that they love. The built in Morality system, as well as the topics of Hunters doing morally objectionable things, being wrong, and even sliding into becoming Slashers all seem to point to a very gray area that they fall into. <br /> <br /> I can see a group running a very black and white version of Hunter where the protagonists are vanquishing monsters for the good of mankind, and actually doing these things in a just manner, but I feel to do so is to dispense with many of core conceits of the game line. <br /> <br /> I feel as though this is a matter of how closely you wish to cling to the game as developed, how you interpret what they have given us, and ultimately how you wish to run your game. No right or wrong answers really, which is the beauty of our hobby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11942-the13thghost","name":"The13thGhost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}